DCS 1
cast WORLD-ZERO
# World Zero, the hub: the cross-realm NPCs (REALM-CASTS.md, build order 1). They stand by the rainbow gates and
# travel them; what they say depends on where the hero has been (shared flags: visited_* set by the realm casts).

who Gate Ferryman Bram
voice 3 0.95
step start
if rode_all -> veteran
if rode -> again
say Four rainbows, four realms, one ferry. I ride with anyone who steps through.
say Gallery City to the east, the Parcels west, Bricks north, the Labyrinth south. The eighth bit is a cube away.
ask Which way, traveller? | East, the galleries=east | West, the farms=west | North or south=more | None yet=stay
step more
ask North or south? | North, the bricks=north | South, the maze=south | Neither=stay
step east
set rode
say Mind the paint. It's still wet in places and the murals talk back.
end
step west
set rode
say Fences, fields and a postmaster who never sleeps. Stamp what he hands you.
end
step north
set rode
say Everything up there snaps together. So do the people, mostly.
end
step south
set rode
say Chalk your route. The maze folds when you stop looking at it.
end
step stay
say The gates keep. So do I.
end
step again
ask Back for another rainbow? | Yes=start | Just talking=chat
step chat
say I've ridden every gate a thousand times and never seen the same sky twice.
end
step veteran
say You've ridden them all. Some day you'll tell me which realm is home.
end

who Rainbow Painter
voice 5 1.05
step start
if gate_east_painted -> painted
say The east rainbow's faded to three bands. A gate needs seven or it drops you short.
ask Fetch me four pots of pigment from the galleries? | I'll find them=accept | Not now=later
step accept
set quest_paint_east
say Any colour the curators spare. Ask for Pigment Crates. I'll mix the rest.
end
step later
say Three bands will hold a week. Maybe two.
end
step painted
say Seven bands. Look at it. That's the way a gate should pour.
end

who Wandering Merchant Zee
voice 1 1.0
step start
if visited_labyrinth -> lab_stock
if visited_bricks -> brick_stock
if visited_parcels -> parcel_stock
if visited_gallery -> gallery_stock
say Zee's cart. Stock follows the roads I've walked, and I walk where you walk.
say Come back once you've been somewhere; I'll have what that somewhere sells.
end
step gallery_stock
say Fresh from the galleries: brushes, varnish, a frame plate or two.
give ZEE_BRUSH 1
end
step parcel_stock
say Farm goods today. Honey, seed, a stamp hammer I didn't ask how they got.
give ZEE_HONEY 1
end
step brick_stock
say Studs and plates, sorted by colour. The kids' club sorted them. Twice.
give ZEE_STUD 2
end
step lab_stock
say Chalk. Thread. A compass that only points at exits. Bargains, all.
give ZEE_CHALK 1
end

who Heartstone Seeker Captain
voice 4 0.9
step start
if heartstone_race -> racing
say Four of us, four realms, four Heartstones. We're ahead of you in all of them.
ask Race us? | You're on=race | I don't race=decline
step race
set heartstone_race
say First to all four. No gates skipped, no stones shared. See you in the galleries.
end
step decline
say Then stay out of our way at the gates.
end
step racing
say We have two. You?
end

who Courier of Worlds
voice 2 1.0
step start
say I carry what you can't: anything, any realm, any gate. Fee's a cube per crossing.
ask Send something? | Send an item east=send | Collect=collect | Nothing today=no
step send
say Hand it over and name the realm. It'll be waiting at that realm's notice board.
end
step collect
say Nothing's come for you yet. The boards would have told me.
end
step no
say The gates are open all night. So am I.
end

who Tugboat Balloonist
voice 6 1.1
step start
if island_towed -> towed
say Islands don't move themselves. Mine does, with a balloon and a very long rope.
say Own a plot you'd rather have nearer the hub? I tow. Lower numbers are dearer, mind.
ask Hire the tug? | Tow my island=hire | Just asking=ask
step hire
set tow_requested
say Mark the deed you want it moved beside. Give me a day and a fair wind.
end
step ask
say Fourteen islands moved last night. Not one of them noticed.
end
step towed
say Settled in? Good. The rope's coiled for the next one.
end
